<title>FINLAND: Nokia says to sell tuner operations.</title>
<headline>Nokia says to sell tuner operations.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecoms group Nokia Oy said in a statement on Friday it would divest its tuner operations.</p>
<p>&quot;Under the agreement, Nokia will sell its Turku tuner factory to Semi-Tech Turku Oy,&quot; Nokia said.</p>
<p>Semi-Tech Turku is part of Hong Kong owned Semi-Tech (Global) Ltd, the investment arm of Toronto-based Semi Tech Corporation.</p>
<p>Nokia said it would continue to develop tuners for multimedia equipment.  </p>
<p>&quot;In the future, these components designed to meet the special needs required by digital transmission technology will be manufactured by subcontractors,&quot; Nokia said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
